# Keep the build context small and, more importantly, HERMETIC. Everything excluded here is
# either maintainer state that must not influence a published image, or bulk that only slows
# the upload of the context to the daemon.
#
# The correctness argument, not just the speed one: node_modules/ and .venv/ contain
# platform-specific compiled artifacts from a Windows dev machine. Copied into a Linux image
# they would either break the build or, worse, half-work. dist/ is excluded so the image can
# never accidentally install a stale wheel sitting in the maintainer's tree instead of the one
# stage 2 just built from source.

.git
.gitattributes
.github

# Maintainer state -- never let a local build artifact reach a published image.
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
src/chronotrace/_ui/
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Caches: large, machine-specific, and meaningless in the image.
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.hypothesis/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Recordings are somebody's program memory. They have no business in a public image, and the
# demo recording is generated during the build from examples/ instead.
recordings/
*.chrono
*.chrono.idx

# Not needed to build or run the demo.
docs/
spikes/
benchmarks/
flamegraphs/
tests/e2e/
frontend/tests/
